{
	"_description": "Canonical physical-key registry. Every key, mouse button and wheel direction a layer can bind is keyed by its W3C UI Events KeyboardEvent.code (the ids Kalamine and Ergo-L use; mouse buttons and wheel directions are pseudo-codes). Each record carries the identifier every driver uses for that physical position, plus its geometry on an ANSI and an ISO full-size board. Single source of truth for physical-key identity: the keymap layer loaders resolve bindings through it, and tools/test/test-physical-keys-registry.cjs pins every older hand copy (evdev.json, azerty.json, heatmap_win.js, the frozen Karabiner legacy_layer_keys.json, kanata.kbd) to it.",
	"_fields": {
		"kind": "key | mouse_button | wheel.",
		"group": "function | alphanumeric | navigation | numpad | media | mouse | wheel.",
		"ahk": "AutoHotkey v2 hotkey name: SCnnn scan code for keys, the key name for mouse buttons and wheel directions.",
		"ahk_send": "AutoHotkey Send name for a layout-independent key, or null for a character key (a Send of a character key uses {SCnnn} so the active layout cannot change which key is pressed).",
		"evdev": "Linux input-event-codes.h KEY_* / BTN_* code; null for a wheel direction (a REL_WHEEL / REL_HWHEEL motion, described by axis and direction).",
		"hs": "macOS virtual keycode (kVK_*) for keys, the NSEvent button number for mouse buttons; null for a wheel direction.",
		"karabiner": "Karabiner-Elements event object ({key_code}, {consumer_key_code} or {pointing_button}); null for a wheel direction, which Karabiner cannot take as input.",
		"kanata": "kanata key name, in the short form every kanata release accepts.",
		"macos_iso": "Overrides for macOS on an ISO keyboard: macOS reports the key left of 1 and the key left of Z with swapped codes (kVK_ISO_Section / kVK_ANSI_Grave, and non_us_backslash / grave_accent_and_tilde in Karabiner).",
		"geometry": "Per form factor (ansi, iso): row (0 = function row), col (left edge, in key units), width, and for a key taller than one row its height; the ISO Enter also gives bottom_col and bottom_width for its narrower lower row. A form a key is absent from has no entry.",
		"axis": "Wheel only: vertical or horizontal.",
		"direction": "Wheel only: +1 for up/right, -1 for down/left."
	},
	"schema_version": 1,
	"forms": ["ansi", "iso"],
